# Keep the deploy to THIS app.
#
# A git worktree lives at icefall-app/.claude/worktrees/*, and Vercel's
# multi-service detection reads it as a second Vite project inside the first —
# which fails the build with an "Invalid vercel.json - `services`" error that
# names a directory nobody deploying this app has ever heard of.
.claude
node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*

# THIRD-PARTY TRADEMARKS AND GENERATED PORTRAITS — the two lines that were missing.
#
# Both directories were listed in .gitignore with the note "never shipped", and
# two comments in src/services/operators.ts asserted they were "gitignored AND
# vercelignored". Only the first half was true. `vercel` deploys from the local
# working directory, not from git, so it copied both folders wholesale.
#
# Measured on the 2026-09-04 preview deployment, all HTTP 200:
#   /img/operators/ee.png   Elite Exped's mark
#   /img/operators/p14.png  14 Peaks Expedition's mark
#   /img/guides/guide-demo-lama.jpg   a generated portrait of an invented guide
#   /img/guides/CREDITS.md  a public file naming all eight invented guides
#
# Four real companies' trademarks (Elite Exped, 14 Peaks, Adventure Consultants,
# Seven Summit Treks) were downloadable by anyone who guessed the path. The
# safety model the code describes — a mark stays on the machine it was put on —
# only works if BOTH ignore files carry it.
#
# Nothing breaks: `CompanyMark` falls back to a monogram when a path is missing
# or fails to load, and GuidePortrait falls back to initials. That fallback is
# what a fresh clone has always rendered.
public/img/operators/
public/img/guides/
